<title>RUSSIA: Russia's Norilsk Nickel falls 11.3 pct on '96 loss.</title>
<headline>Russia's Norilsk Nickel falls 11.3 pct on '96 loss.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian metals mining concern Norilsk Nickel fell 11.3 percent by 0945 GMT on Monday to $6.500 from $7.33 at Friday's close, but up from $6.35 earlier.</p>
<p>Traders said Friday's announcement of a 3.29 trillion rouble consolidated loss in 1996 by the company, Russia's most significant producer of nickel, platinum group metals and cobalt, dragged down both Nickel and the market overall.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
